{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>But the chief cupbearer did not remember Joseph, and he forgot him.</b> For one transgression draws another: at first, even though Joseph did come to his mind, nevertheless he did not remember him before Pharaoh for good — and this caused that in the end he forgot him entirely, so that he did not even come to mind. And concerning these two transgressions he said, ״אֶת חֲטָאַי אֲנִי מַזְכִּיר הַיּוֹם״ (Genesis 41:9) — that is, these two sins: that which he sinned against Joseph and against Pharaoh. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 89:3) that Joseph sinned in this, that he placed his trust in the chief cupbearer, and he used the language of remembrance twice: ״כִּי אִם זְכַרְתַּנִי״ and so forth (Genesis 40:14), ״וְהִזְכַּרְתַּנִי״ and so forth (ibid.) — and corresponding to them he was punished with a double forgetting: ״וְלֹא זָכַר שַׂר הַמַּשְׁקִים אֶת יוֹסֵף וַיִּשְׁכָּחֵהוּ״ (Genesis 40:23)." "And by way of allusion we may say: at the time that Joseph said ״אִם זְכַרְתַּנִי״ — and this is the language of a condition, as if he said, 'If you remember me, there is hope; and if not, hope is lost' — it turns out that these two words comprise the essence of the sin. Therefore, corresponding to them, a heavenly echo went forth and said ״תִּשְׁכַּח״, for ״תִּשְׁכַּח״ has the same numerical value as ״אִם זְכַרְתַּנִי״. And therefore the decree was given that he would remain imprisoned yet another two years, for the days of the year are 365 days; twice 365 equals 730, which is the numerical value of ״תִּשְׁכַּח״. And therefore the decree dictates that he remain imprisoned yet two full years, for ״מִקֵּץ שְׁנָתַיִם יָמִים״ (Genesis 41:1) indicates that they were complete years from day to day, so as to fill the numerical value of ״תִּשְׁכַּח״, plus two additional days corresponding to these two words that he said: ״וְהִזְכַּרְתַּנִי״ ״וְהוֹצֵאתַנִי״. And this is more clearly elucidated than what some have said, that these two years correspond to these two words — which is difficult: why specifically years and not months or days? But according to our approach, it is truly two days that correspond to them, and this will be explained further nearby in the portion of מִקֵּץ, with the help of the Blessed Name."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "Genesis Rabbah citation normalized from פט,ג to 89:3.", 1 "״תִּשְׁכַּח״ = ת(400)+ש(300)+כ(20)+ח(8) = 728, not 730; ״אִם זְכַרְתַּנִי״ = א(1)+ם(40)+ז(7)+כ(20)+ר(200)+ת(400)+נ(50)+י(10) = 728. The figures match each other at 728, though the text states 730 (twice 365). Translated as written. The final abbreviation בע״ה expanded per convention as 'with the help of the Blessed Name.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:50.374478050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}